---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import GpuVisual from "./GpuVisual.astro";
---

<section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="status-dot"></span> GPU PERFORMANCE ENGINEERING
    </div>
    <h1 id="hero-title">
      Your LLM probably
      <br class="desktop-break" /> doesn’t need
      <br /> more GPUs.
      <br />
      <span class="text-accent">Fewer bottlenecks.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-description">
      I optimize LLM inference from serving stack to GPU kernel — CUDA, Triton,
      vLLM, FlashInfer, PyTorch, and the ugly parts in between.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="#audit">
        Request a Performance Audit <Icon name="external" size={18} />
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="#services">
        See what I optimize <Icon size={18} />
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-footnote-row">
      <p class="hero-footnote mono">
        PROFILE FIRST. OPTIMIZE SECOND. SCALE THIRD.
      </p>
      <button class="motion-toggle mono" aria-pressed="false">
        PAUSE MOTION
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <GpuVisual />
  <div class="hero-bottom">
    <span class="mono">CLOSER TO THE METAL. FURTHER FROM THE HYPE.</span>
    <a class="scroll-cue mono" href="#story">
      SCROLL TO INVESTIGATE <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="tech-strip">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="mono tech-label">THE WORKING SET</span>
    <span>CUDA</span>
    <span>Triton</span>
    <span>vLLM</span>
    <span>FlashInfer</span>
    <span>PyTorch</span>
    <span>CuTe</span>
    <span class="mono tech-tail">// BUILT BELOW THE ABSTRACTION</span>
  </div>
</div>
